```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <title>Login Page</title>
  <script>
    function submitForm() {
      const username = document.getElementById('username').value;
      const password = document.getElementById('password').value;

      if (username.trim() === "" || password.trim() === "") {
        alert("Username and password are required.");
        return;
      }

      // Example: Simulate login to backend (replace with actual server call)
      fetch('/login', {
        method: 'POST',
        headers: {
          'Content-Type': 'application/json'
        },
        body: JSON.stringify({ username, password })
      })
      .then(response => response.json())
      .then(data => {
        if (data.success) {
          alert("Login success!��" + data.message);
          // Redirect or handle further actions
        } else {
          alert("Login failed: " + data.message);
        }
      })
      .catch(err => {
        alert("Error: " + err.message);
      });
    }

    document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {
      const loginForm = document.getElementById('login-form');
      loginForm.addEventListener('submit', submitForm);
    });
  </script>
</head>
<body>
  <h2>Login</h2>
  <form id="login-form">
    <input type="text" id="username" placeholder="Enter username" required />
    <input type="password" id="password" placeholder="Enter password" required />
    <button type="submit">Login</button>
  </form>
</body>
</html>
```

### Notes:
- This code creates a simple form for user login, with validation.
- The `submitForm` function handles form submission and sends credentials to a backend server.
- Replace `/login` with your actual server endpoint or backend URL.
- Ensure the server-side script (e.g., `login.php`, `api/login.php`) is properly configured to process the request.
